KAE Debian source layout
========================

The upstream KAE repository stores these files in scripts/debian. The
`bash build.sh debpack` entry point copies the working source into a unique
kae_output/debpack/run.XXXXXX/source directory and moves the packaging copy to
its root debian directory before invoking dpkg-buildpackage. The original
checkout keeps scripts/debian only. Build output and failed builds remain in
that run directory, outside the disposable kae_build staging directory used
by RPM builds. Remove old run directories explicitly when no longer needed.

In the Ubuntu packaging repository, move scripts/debian to the root debian
directory and maintain only that copy. Internal packaging paths deliberately
use the standard debian/ layout. The debpack wrapper synchronizes the upstream
version from VERSION before calling dpkg-buildpackage without another copy.
For direct dpkg-buildpackage use, run python3 debian/prepare-version.py first.
This retains the Debian revision, distribution and previous changelog entries.
Source uploads should be prepared from this standard Ubuntu layout; the orig
archive must match it as well.

The binary build uses the running 6.8 ARM64 kernel and its configured headers.
Custom kernel headers cannot be named generically in Build-Depends; they must
be provisioned before building. For a distribution builder, declare the exact
headers dependency in the publishing branch and set KERNEL_RELEASE/KERNEL_DIR.
The debpack wrapper resolves a relative KERNEL_DIR from the caller's working
directory and reports an invalid or inaccessible directory before staging.
The builder's host kernel must not be mistaken for the deployment kernel.
Install the other dependencies listed in control before running the build.

Upstream patch scripts and bundled compression archives are reused in a
private debian/.build/source tree. No network downloads or module operations
are needed during the build. The parent checkout remains unchanged.

Use an orig.tar matching the complete upstream snapshot, including the shared
package build scripts and the root VERSION file. If using an older upstream
release tarball instead, represent its upstream-file differences as quilt
patches in debian/patches.
Generated objects, staged packages and debian/.build are not source files.
